"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Gives appropriate directions to places taking into account the type of interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Describing Places with Prepositions of Place"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you describe places, you use prepositions of place like <span class=\"italic\">through, on </span> or <span class=\"italic\"> at.</span> <br><br>You go <span class=\"strong\">through</span>  a space, like a park or a market.<br>You walk <span class=\"strong\">on</span>  a street.<br>You use <span class=\"strong\">at</span>  to talk about a place, like a pub."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You can walk through the market."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are street jugglers and musicians on every street."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You can have a snack or something to drink at a local pub."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Near, Close, Far"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the adjectives <span class=\"strong\">near</span>, <span class=\"strong\">close</span> and <span class=\"strong\">far</span> to say the distance of one thing or place to another.<br><br><span class=\"italic\">Near</span>  and <span class=\"italic\">close</span>  have the same meaning. <span class=\"italic\">Far</span>  has the opposite meaning <br><br> The expression <span class=\"italic\">too far</span> means something is very far in a negative way.<br><br>You often talk about how far something is using the time it takes to walk or drive.  A hyphen ( - ) goes between the number and the word <span class=\"italic\">minute</span> or <span class=\"italic\">hour</span>, like  <span class=\"italic\">10-minute drive.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Is the market far? <br> <span class=\"strong\">Tourist Agent</span>: No, it's very close. It's about a 10-minute walk."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: How far is the airport? <br><span class=\"strong\">Tourist Agent</span>: It's not far either. It's a 15-minute drive."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "antique"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a very old object"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will find art, antiques, food, and fashion in the market."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when you visit a city."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pub "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a bar where you can order food"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can have a snack or something to drink at a local pub."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "atmosphere"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "environment; mood of a place"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's a great spot to experience the London atmosphere."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to have a story to tell"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "many interesting things have happened"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Every building has a story to tell."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "center "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "most important place"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Covent Garden is also the theater center of London."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "juggler "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a performer who throws and catches objects"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are street jugglers and musicians on every street."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "walk "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "The time it takes to walk to a place "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The market is a 10-minute walk."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "drive"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "The time it takes to drive to a place"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The airport is a 15-minute drive."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob01aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le08ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online to learn about other places to see and things to do in London."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue giving suggestions. You work at the tourist office. Your partner is a tourist."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice your dialogue."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about London."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a dialogue asking for and giving suggestions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice a dialogue on suggestions between a tourist and a guide."}]}], "type": "sena"}